   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Blue Mule**: rare: 14 archived performances [9]\n- **Sitting In Limbo**: back after 157 archived shows (639 days); rare: 8 archived performances [9]\n- **Salty Dog**: rare: 8 archived performances [9]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2019-09-28.matrix.flac24** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 22 songs; 128 min; rated 5/5 by 5 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer praises the recording and mastering as superb; Reviewer calls the recording spectacular [6][8]\n- **billystrings2019-09-28.dpa4022.flac24**: source not stated; 23 songs; 122 min [2]\n- **billystrings2019-09-28.dpa4022.flac16**: source not stated; 23 songs; 122 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer says this is the best-sounding recording of Billy's shows they have heard, having attended many [7]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2019-09-28.matrix.flac24**: taped by John Hermsen; transferred by John Hermsen; source: AKG C568 EB + Nak CP4 + DPA 4080 > Sound Devices Mixpre 6 [1]. Also: Recorded and transferred by John Hermsen using AKG C568EB, Nakamichi CM300 with CP4 shotguns (Sank P48 mod), and DPA 4080 microphones into a Sound Devices MixPre 6; Mastering was done by Markus W. in Dusseldorf, Germany [1]\n- **billystrings2019-09-28.dpa4022.flac24**: taped by John Hermsen; transferred by gilde; source: DOA 4022 > Sound Devices 722 [2]. Also: Captured on a Sound Devices 722 at 24-bit/48kHz, then processed with Waves L3 Ultramaximizer for limiting, dither and noise shaping [2]\n- **billystrings2019-09-28.dpa4022.flac16**: taped by John Hermsen; transferred by gilde; source: DPA 4022 > Sound Devices 722 [3]. Also: Sound Devices 722 recording at 24-bit/48kHz, resampled to 44.1kHz with iZotope, then Waves L3 Ultramaximizer applied [3]",
